NAMRBD Licensing
================

Unless a file or directory contains a different license notice, NAMRBD source
code and documentation are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The Linux kernel module sources under:

  kernel/module/

are licensed under GPL-2.0-only. Those files carry SPDX license identifiers and
must remain compatible with the Linux kernel module licensing boundary.

Vendored or forked third-party source retains its upstream license. The
NAMRBD-managed gotgt fork under:

  third_party/gotgt/

preserves the upstream Apache-2.0 license and keeps NAMRBD patch notes in
`third_party/gotgt/NAMRBD_PATCHES.md`.

License texts are provided under `LICENSES/`:

  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
  LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt
  LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt

This file describes the repository license policy. It is not a substitute for
the license notices embedded in individual files or third-party directories.
